From 7c99e80aa111b7a658155b6ccc822cf39ab9ec84 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 15:27:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: gc2145: Add the white balance and 3A lock controls

Nothing could freeze the AEC and the AWB, and nothing could read out or
set the white balance, so there was no way to settle a preview and then
reproduce it on a full resolution still: switching format restarted both
algorithms from scratch.

Both of them hand their result registers back when switched off, keeping
whatever they last converged on, so switching them off is a real 3A lock
rather than an approximation of one, and it is also how manual mode is
entered. Wire V4L2_CID_3A_LOCK to that, and add the white balance as an
auto cluster whose gains read back what the AWB settled on.

The preset gains are the ones every vendor register table carries.

Also add exposure metering, which picks whether the AEC weights its
centre window, and delete the block of controls that was disabled with
an #if 0: it came from a different sensor and none of the registers it
named exist on this one.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
